# Build inputs are tracked, not ignored. `poetry.lock` and `pyproject.toml` were
# previously listed here, which meant the repository carried no dependency
# manifest at all: `requirements.txt` was the only checked-in pin set, nothing
# recorded the declared (as opposed to resolved) dependencies, and a fresh clone
# could not reproduce the environment the notebooks were written against.
# Commit both files instead.

# Credentials: never tracked. See client/kalshi_client.py for the expected
# format, and prefer KALSHI_CREDENTIALS_PATH to keep the file outside the
# checkout entirely.
client/credentials.yaml
.env

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
